{
  "id": "delayed-auditory-feedback",
  "term": "delayed auditory feedback",
  "definition": "Delayed auditory feedback is an experimental condition in which a person hears their own speech played back with a short delay, usually through headphones. This delayed self-hearing often disrupts fluent speaking by slowing speech and increasing disfluencies or speech errors, and its effects depend not only on timing mismatch but also on the speech-like content of the feedback.",
